# Title Master — test SKU

**Default test SKU:** `SP 12120 4OHM GTR`  
(Config: `config/marketplace_testing.php` → `title_sku`)

## Safe testing order

1. Dry-run (no API writes):
   `php artisan marketplace:audit-master title --dry-run --sku="SP 12120 4OHM GTR"`
2. Single marketplace dry-run:
   `php artisan marketplace:audit-master title --dry-run --sku="SP 12120 4OHM GTR" --marketplace=amazon`
3. Live push only after dry-run passes (confirmation required):
   - Per-tile: `POST /api/marketplaces/push-single` with `{ sku, marketplace, title_type, title }`
   - Title 150 bulk (row/toolbar): `POST /api/marketplaces/push-title` with `{ sku, title }`
   - Or: `php artisan marketplace:audit-master title --live --sku="SP 12120 4OHM GTR" --marketplace=amazon`

## Push wiring (24 channels)

- Registry: `AllMarketplaceChannelRegistry::titleMeta()` — tiers 150 / 100 / 80 / 60
- API dispatch: `MarketplaceTitlePushService::push()` (all 24 push keys)
- Validation: `pushSingleMarketplace` uses `titlePushKeys()` + `titleTypeForMarketplace()` (not hardcoded lists)
- **Distribute ALL** pushes all `titlePushKeysForType('150')` (15 channels), not legacy Amazon/Temu/Reverb/Wayfair only

## Known status for this SKU (dry-run)

- **Wiring:** 24/24 marketplaces ready (credentials + service)
- **Content:** PM titles present (`title150`, `title100`, `title80`, `title60` per tier)
- **Metrics rows:** ebay, ebay3, temu, doba, walmart; blank metrics title columns do not block push when PM has content
- **ebay2:** no `item_id` in metrics; eBay API lookup on push
- **aliexpress:** no `product_id` in `aliexpress_metric`; live push may fail until synced

Do not run bulk or multi-marketplace live pushes without explicit user approval.
